{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C2","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C2","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Board switcher changes view, URL param persists selection","impl_has":"Board switcher renders as anchor links with /?board={id}. URL param board persists as GET param on navigation. Board tab switching uses GET /?board=N and /activity?board=N. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:1470-1484","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C3","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-C3","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Three-tier visibility: haven -> MQTT export. world -> MQTT export + world flag queryable. private -> no export.","impl_has":"Visibility tiers are enforced in storage and MCP. ExportModule forwards haven/world boards to external bus. However: world flag 'queryable by external scrapers' has no implementation — board_list_boards returns visibility field but there is no dedicated scraper endpoint or world-discovery API. The spec acknowledges the scraper is out-of-scope ('world publisher/scraper process is out of scope for this spec'), making this acceptable.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2699-2778","recommendation":"MQTT export path is implemented. World scraper is explicitly out-of-scope per spec. Downgrade to P3 informational — no action needed on impl. Verify that ExportModule actually publishes over MQTT in integrated mode (standalone mode falls back to no-op at line 2774-2778).","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C4","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P1","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-C4","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Board with visibility=private -> no MQTT messages, not visible to other participants","impl_has":"_on_board_event checks visibility field from event data (line 2749-2751) and skips export if private. board_status MCP gates private boards to owner only (line 2505-2507). Board page GET does NOT enforce visibility — any user with network access to port 8889 can query /?board=N for any board_id regardless of owner or visibility. This is a web UI gap, not MCP.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2082-2133","recommendation":"Web UI has no visibility enforcement. The board page GET at line 2133 calls render_board_page(db, board_id) with no visibility check — a user can read any board by guessing its integer ID. Add a visibility/ownership check before rendering. Acceptable for single-user standalone mode but breaks multi-tenancy for web UI.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C5","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C5","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Click expand icon -> minor items show/hide","impl_has":"toggleMajorAccordion JS function at line 1820 controls minor item visibility per major task. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:1820-1835","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

