{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C11","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"mcp_parity","spec_ref":"BM-C11","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Every UI action has a corresponding MCP tool","impl_has":"17 MCP tools cover all StorageModule operations. Gap 1: Web UI has a /set-visibility POST route and a visibility dropdown directly on the board page, which maps to board_set_visibility MCP tool — this is covered. Gap 2: Web UI 'edit task' action (name + notes) maps to board_rename_task + board_update MCP tools separately, not a single 'board_edit_task' tool. The edit operation is achievable via MCP but requires two calls. Gap 3: board_manage_board action enum is ['create','rename','delete'] but does not include a 'set_visibility' action — that is a separate board_set_visibility tool, which is correct per spec table.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2381-2463","recommendation":"MCP parity is structurally complete. The two-call workaround for edit (rename + update) is acceptable — document that board_update accepts notes field for this use case. No new tool needed, but the spec could note this equivalence explicitly.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

