{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C13","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C13","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"POST /api/v1/apps/board-manager/deploy -> container running","impl_has":"Deployment via service hub is out of scope for the implementation file — this is a deployment concern. No Dockerfile or compose.yaml visible in this single-file analysis, but the spec references these as separate artifacts. Cannot verify from board_manager.py alone.","impl_file":"N/A","recommendation":"Needs manual review of deployment artifacts (Dockerfile, board-manager.compose.yaml). Out of scope for this analysis.","status":"needs_manual_review","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C14","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"bus_integration","spec_ref":"BM-C14","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Exported board changes -> MQTT messages published","impl_has":"ExportModule._on_board_event calls self.publish_external() at line 2775. In standalone mode (no composeio framework), this is a no-op (AppModule stub at line 66). MQTT connectivity only activates when the real composeio framework is loaded via HAS_COMPOSEIO=True. The create_app() call at line 2834 invokes connect_transport() which is also a stub in standalone mode.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2774-2778","recommendation":"MQTT export is framework-dependent. In standalone/dev mode, exports silently do nothing. This is by design but should be surfaced in logs. Add a warning log when publish_external is called but HAS_COMPOSEIO is False, so operators know the export layer is inactive.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C15","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C15","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Container restart -> all data intact","impl_has":"DB_PATH defaults to /app/data/board_manager.db. Docker volume mount at /app/data ensures persistence. SQLite WAL mode enabled. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:143-147","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C16","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C16","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Log entry via MCP -> entry appears in Activity tab","impl_has":"board_log_activity MCP tool calls storage.log_activity which INSERTs to activity_log. Activity tab at /activity reads from activity_log. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:858-874","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C17","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C17","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Visual inspection: charcoal bg, teal/red/amber status","impl_has":"CSS vars: --md-bg:#2b2b2b (charcoal), --md-primary:#4051b5 (indigo), --md-green:#00c853, --md-red:#ff5252, --md-amber:#ffc107. Dark theme is slate/indigo consistent with Material for MkDocs palette. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:979-987","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C18","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"multi_tenancy","spec_ref":"BM-C18","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Intelligence A cannot modify Intelligence B's board via MCP","impl_has":"_check_ownership() enforces board ownership for all MCP mutating tools (board_add_task, board_update, board_rename_task, board_delete_task, board_archive_task, board_set_target_date, board_attach_document, board_detach_document, board_manage_objective, board_log_activity, board_reorder_tasks, board_set_visibility, board_manage_board rename/delete). Gap: _get_caller_identity() defaults to 'david' (line 2478) when no _caller_identity or owner_id is in arguments. This means a caller that omits identity silently succeeds as 'david', not fails. BM-C18 is met only when callers pass identity explicitly.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2476-2478","recommendation":"The default fallback to 'david' undermines multi-tenancy enforcement. Change the default to None and return a 401-equivalent error if identity is missing and the operation is mutating. Accept the 'david' default only for board_status and board_list_boards (read operations). This is a behavioral gap for BM-C18.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C19","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"multi_tenancy","spec_ref":"BM-C19","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"MCP board_manage_board(create) without Haven identity -> rejected","impl_has":"board_manage_board action=create checks `if not caller:` at line 2604. But _get_caller_identity() never returns None or empty — it defaults to 'david'. So the check `if not caller` will never trigger. A caller that passes no identity at all will create a board under 'david', not be rejected. The rejection only fires if _caller_identity is explicitly set to an empty string.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2598-2608","recommendation":"Same root cause as gap-BM-C18. Fix _get_caller_identity() to return None when identity is absent, not 'david'. Then the `if not caller` check at line 2604 will work as intended. This is a P1 correctness gap for the stated compliance criterion.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C20","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-C20","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Board set to haven -> appears on MQTT. Set to private -> disappears from MQTT.","impl_has":"set_visibility calls refresh_subscriptions() when changing from private to haven/world (line 604-606). This adds new subscriptions. Gap: when changing from haven/world BACK to private, no unsubscribe occurs. The ExportModule's _on_board_event does check visibility from event data and skips private boards (line 2749-2751), so events won't be forwarded even if subscription exists. This makes the 'disappears from MQTT' behavior functionally correct but the subscription bookkeeping is leaky.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:596-607","recommendation":"The functional behavior is correct (event data check prevents forwarding). The leaky subscription is cosmetic. Add an unsubscribe path in refresh_subscriptions() to be explicit. Low urgency.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C21","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"compliance","spec_ref":"BM-C21","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"board_list_boards returns own boards + haven/world boards from others","impl_has":"fetch_boards(db, owner_id=caller) returns WHERE owner_id=? OR visibility IN ('haven','world'). This is exactly the spec requirement. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:358-364","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-C22","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-C22","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Two owners with 'backlog' board -> separate namespace subtrees on MQTT","impl_has":"ExportModule._on_board_event constructs export_ns = f'board/{owner}/{safe_name}/{category}' using board.owner as namespace prefix. Two owners with same board name produce different namespaces. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2772","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-compliance","area":"compliance_items","total_gaps":10,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":5,"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED":5},"by_priority":{"P1":3,"P2":2,"P3":5},"notes":"10 of 22 compliance items have gaps. 12 are compliant and closed. Three P1 issues: web UI visibility not enforced (BM-C4), MCP identity default undermines ownership (BM-C18/C19). Two P2 issues: MCP parity gap on edit-task (BM-C11), MQTT export is no-op in standalone (BM-C14)."}

