### Edit Task Popup (Name + Notes, Save Button)

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-UI-EDIT-TASK-POPUP","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"edit_task_popup","spec_ref":"BM-UI-LAYOUT","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"edit icon opens an 'Edit Task' popup with fields for task name and notes (textarea). Submit button labeled 'Save'. Used for both major and minor tasks.","impl_has":"The edit icon on both major and minor rows links to /rename?id={task_id} (GET). The /rename route calls render_rename_form() which renders _page_edit_task(). This function produces a full page (not an inline popup) with title 'Edit Task', name input, notes textarea, Cancel link, and a 'Save' button (btn-primary). The page navigates away from the board and back. The Save button label is correct. The two fields (name, notes) are correct. The distinction is: spec says 'popup', implementation uses a dedicated page (full navigation).","impl_file":"board_manager.py:1258-1259, 1603-1611, 1907-1923","recommendation":"The edit task form is functionally correct — name, notes, Save button are all present and work. The spec explicitly says 'popup' but the implementation uses a full-page navigation pattern consistent with the rename/delete/reorder pages. This is a presentation gap, not a functional one. Options: (1) Accept the full-page pattern and update spec to say 'dedicated page or popup', or (2) Refactor edit-task to an inline overlay popup like the New Board popup. Given that the spec was written as a target, either is valid. Recommend updating spec to 'dedicated page' for consistency with the rest of the edit flows.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

