### Tab Switching Performance (BM-UI-PERFORMANCE)

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-UI-PERF-INDEXES","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"tab_switching_performance","spec_ref":"BM-UI-PERFORMANCE","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Optimize by: (1) pre-computing activity counts, (2) limiting default activity query to 24h, (3) using lightweight queries for tab content not immediately visible.","impl_has":"(1) Activity counts are pre-computed with a batched IN query via fetch_activity_counts_for_tasks(db, task_ids) at line 482-490 — not a per-task query, one batch query. (2) render_activity_page defaults to interval='24h' at line 2095 and fetch_activity defaults to 24h. (3) Four performance indexes created at init_db(): idx_activity_log_created_at, idx_activity_log_task_id, idx_tasks_board_id, idx_tasks_parent_id. All three spec recommendations are implemented. Compliant.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:250-257, 482-490, 439-446","recommendation":"Performance optimization points from spec are addressed. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-UI-PERF-DOC-COUNTS","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"tab_switching_performance","spec_ref":"BM-UI-PERFORMANCE","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Tab switching MUST complete in under 500ms — optimize queries.","impl_has":"fetch_document_counts(db) at line 469-473 executes SELECT task_id, COUNT(*) FROM task_documents GROUP BY task_id with NO board_id filter. This scans all task_documents across all tenants on every board page load. In a multi-tenant deployment with many boards and attachments, this becomes a full table scan. The result is returned as a dict keyed by task_id, so only the current board's task IDs will be used — but the query pulls everything.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:469-473","recommendation":"Scope fetch_document_counts to the current board: pass board_id and add JOIN tasks t ON task_documents.task_id=t.id WHERE t.board_id=? This keeps the board page query set fully scoped. Low urgency in single-user mode but becomes meaningful with many tenants.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-performance","area":"tab_switching_performance","total_gaps":1,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":1},"by_priority":{"P2":1},"notes":"Three of four spec-recommended optimizations are implemented. One residual gap: fetch_document_counts is cross-tenant. Indexes are in place. The 500ms target should be achievable in single-tenant mode; multi-tenant mode may require the scoping fix."}

