### MCP Parity (BM-C11)

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-MCP-PARITY-FULL","category":"SPEC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"mcp_parity","spec_ref":"BM-MCP","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Full MCP parity with all web UI capabilities. 17 tools listed in spec table.","impl_has":"MCP_TOOLS list contains exactly 17 tools matching all names in the spec table. Each tool is implemented in mcp_handle_tool_call. Compliant on tool count and names.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2381-2463","recommendation":"Compliant. Close.","status":"closed","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-MCP-BOARD-NAME-RESOLVE","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"mcp_parity","spec_ref":"BM-MCP","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"All tools accept board_id or board (name) to target a specific board.","impl_has":"_resolve_board_id() at line 2466-2473 handles both board_id and board (name). If board name not found, defaults to board_id=1 (Maker board). This silent default-to-1 fallback could cause confusing behavior if a tool is called with a board name that doesn't exist — it silently operates on board 1 instead of returning an error.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2466-2473","recommendation":"The silent fallback to board_id=1 when board name is not found is a latent bug. Return an error if board name is provided but not found, rather than defaulting to board 1. This is especially important in multi-tenant mode where a wrong board name should not silently operate on another owner's board.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

