### Multi-Tenancy Enforcement (BM-C18, BM-C19)

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-TENANT-IDENTITY-DEFAULT","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"multi_tenancy","spec_ref":"BM-TENANT","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"MCP tools enforce ownership: mutating tools check that caller's Haven identity matches board owner.","impl_has":"_get_caller_identity() at line 2476-2478: returns arguments.get('_caller_identity', arguments.get('owner_id', 'david')). The triple-level fallback means an MCP caller that passes no identity fields at all is treated as 'david'. For BM-C18: Intelligence B calling board_add_task on Intelligence A's board will be rejected only if B passes its own identity. If B passes no identity, it silently acts as 'david'. For BM-C19: board_manage_board create checks `if not caller:` but caller is never falsy due to the 'david' default.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2476-2478, 2598-2608","recommendation":"This is the same root cause as gap-BM-C18 and gap-BM-C19 above. Single fix: remove the 'david' default from _get_caller_identity(). Return arguments.get('_caller_identity') or arguments.get('owner_id') — no fallback. Mutating operations with no identity should return {ok: False, error: 'Haven identity required'}. Read operations (board_status, board_list_boards, board_get_activity, board_get_documents) can continue to accept anonymous callers.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-TENANT-WEB-HARDCODED","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P2","area":"multi_tenancy","spec_ref":"BM-TENANT","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Board ownership maps to Haven identity. Access control follows Haven governance.","impl_has":"Web UI hardcodes web_owner='david' at line 2086 with comment 'web auth is a future concern'. This means the web UI is single-tenant by design for now — any web UI user operates as 'david'. The spec states multi-tenant support but the web auth layer is not implemented. This is explicitly acknowledged in the code as technical debt.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2085-2086","recommendation":"The hardcoded identity is a known gap, acknowledged in code comments. This is acceptable for Phase 1 (single-user deployment). Track as a spec-acknowledged limitation. Document in spec under BM-TENANT that 'web UI identity is fixed in Phase 1; Phase 2 requires session-based Haven authentication'.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-multi-tenancy","area":"multi_tenancy","total_gaps":2,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":1,"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED":1},"by_priority":{"P1":1,"P2":1},"notes":"Multi-tenancy enforcement is structurally in place but has a critical bypass: the identity default to 'david' makes BM-C18 and BM-C19 non-enforceable without explicit caller identity. Web UI hardcoding is acknowledged tech debt."}

