{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-VIS-WEB-UNPROTECTED","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P1","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-C4","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Private board -> not visible to other participants","impl_has":"Web UI GET / renders any board by integer ID with no visibility or ownership check. A network-accessible user (or Intelligence with HTTP access) can call /?board=2 to read a private board owned by a different user. The MCP board_status correctly gates private boards. The web UI does not.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:2132-2133","recommendation":"Add visibility enforcement in the GET / and GET /activity routes: if board.visibility == 'private' and board.owner_id != web_owner: return 403 page. This is the same fix needed for BM-C4 and BM-C18 web enforcement.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-BM-EXPORT-BUS-EVENT-SCHEMA","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"export_visibility","spec_ref":"BM-BUS-EVENTS","spec_file":"14-board-manager.smd","spec_says":"Event schema includes: event, board, owner, task_id, task_name, parent, field, old_value, new_value, timestamp","impl_has":"StorageModule._publish_change produces events with: event_type, board, board_id, owner, visibility, timestamp, plus operation-specific fields. The 'parent' field (parent task name) is not included in any event. 'field', 'old_value', 'new_value' are only included in rename_task and set_target_date events, not in update_task (which logs `fields: list(fields.keys())` instead of per-field old/new values). The spec example JSON shows a single field change with old/new — impl logs a list of changed field names without values.","impl_file":"board_manager.py:518-550","recommendation":"For full spec compliance, update_task should emit per-field old/new events (one event per changed field, or an array of {field, old_value, new_value} objects). The 'parent' field should be populated by joining to the parent task name. This is a data richness gap affecting subscribers that depend on diff-style events. Medium priority — affects external bus consumers, not internal functionality.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

